@*
    Example 1 — Basic usage.

    A search for "foo" performs a GET to "/?foo". Every user-facing string
    is a parameter: the trigger, the field, and the ⏎ button each get a
    localisable accessible name. Placeholder is optional and has no
    default, because a default would be a hardcoded English string.

    An interactive render mode is required. Under static SSR the markup
    renders, but no event handler runs, so the button cannot open the
    panel.
*@

@page "/examples/search-picker/basic"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using LilyDesignSystem.Blazor.Helpers

<SearchPicker Label="Search this site"
              InputLabel="Search terms"
              SubmitLabel="Search"
              Placeholder="Search…" />
